1
00:00:02,891 --> 00:00:04,863
Hello everyone!
Today: "hopping on wheel".

2
00:00:04,929 --> 00:00:11,588
[Music]

3
00:00:11,654 --> 00:00:14,228
This trick isn't actually that hard.

4
00:00:14,421 --> 00:00:18,107
Of course, you first need
to master regular hops on the pedals.

5
00:00:23,711 --> 00:00:27,624
A good first step,
though optional, is to hop

6
00:00:27,936 --> 00:00:30,630
on the pedals or cranks "seat out".

7
00:00:34,874 --> 00:00:38,294
Along the same lines,
it's worth learning to jump straight

8
00:00:38,333 --> 00:00:40,427
onto the pedals or cranks
and carry on with small hops.

9
00:00:40,493 --> 00:00:48,738
[Music]

10
00:00:48,804 --> 00:00:51,783
Now, in practice,
how do you do this trick?

11
00:00:53,984 --> 00:00:57,484
Obviously, since both hands
are busy holding the saddle,

12
00:00:57,550 --> 00:00:58,878
you can't hold on to anything.

13
00:00:59,077 --> 00:01:01,484
So stay well away from walls

14
00:01:01,810 --> 00:01:04,757
or anything that could hit your back
or head if you fall.

15
00:01:04,797 --> 00:01:06,151
Set up in the middle of flat ground.

16
00:01:06,504 --> 00:01:09,146
For your first hops, it's fine,
and even recommended,

17
00:01:09,170 --> 00:01:13,805
to have a friend, a coach, or anyone
hold you at the hips here.

18
00:01:14,004 --> 00:01:17,064
They can hold on tight
or just stand by in case.

19
00:01:17,277 --> 00:01:20,563
And if you fall, they'll catch you
or at least break your fall.

20
00:01:23,751 --> 00:01:26,677
For "hopping on wheel",
keep three rules in mind.

21
00:01:27,671 --> 00:01:29,411
Rule one: keep your feet tight.

22
00:01:30,384 --> 00:01:32,764
Rule two: land with your legs straight.

23
00:01:33,777 --> 00:01:34,858
Rule three, the last one:

24
00:01:35,084 --> 00:01:37,644
your body leans slightly forward
over the unicycle.

25
00:01:38,604 --> 00:01:40,757
So, I hold the unicycle straight
in front of me,

26
00:01:41,041 --> 00:01:43,321
and the first step is to hop
with your feet tight.

27
00:01:43,387 --> 00:01:49,488
[Music]

28
00:01:49,554 --> 00:01:51,821
Think of hopping a bit higher,

29
00:01:52,087 --> 00:01:53,608
keep your feet tight against the frame,

30
00:01:53,941 --> 00:01:56,274
and they're bound to land
against the wheel.

31
00:01:57,101 --> 00:01:59,254
Don't be too scared, but put both feet on.

32
00:01:59,427 --> 00:02:01,694
If you only put one on,
that's when you risk falling.

33
00:02:02,301 --> 00:02:05,660
Rule two matters too:
land with your legs straight.

34
00:02:08,354 --> 00:02:09,641
If your legs are bent,

35
00:02:09,707 --> 00:02:11,973
it's much less comfortable
and doesn't work as well.

36
00:02:16,561 --> 00:02:17,655
Rule three, the last one:

37
00:02:17,887 --> 00:02:20,474
your body leans slightly forward
over the unicycle.

38
00:02:21,247 --> 00:02:24,700
The unicycle is straight,
and the position looks like this.

39
00:02:26,394 --> 00:02:30,060
I'm on my toes,
and I put all my weight forward.

40
00:02:35,037 --> 00:02:36,237
In this position,

41
00:02:36,287 --> 00:02:39,660
imagine you're pulling
your head forward a tiny bit.

42
00:02:41,427 --> 00:02:44,321
Keep these three positions in mind,

43
00:02:44,360 --> 00:02:46,747
and at first, just touch the wheel
and come back down.

44
00:02:50,274 --> 00:02:53,936
Once you're comfortable with that,
add a second hop,

45
00:02:53,960 --> 00:02:58,273
feel the tire's natural bounce
and settle into that rhythm.

46
00:03:02,621 --> 00:03:03,802
You can guess what's next:

47
00:03:03,914 --> 00:03:06,660
you do two hops,
then three, then four, then fifteen.

48
00:03:06,726 --> 00:03:14,608
[Music]

49
00:03:14,674 --> 00:03:16,074
Once you can do about fifteen

50
00:03:16,100 --> 00:03:19,527
or twenty hops like this,
you can have fun spinning around,

51
00:03:19,967 --> 00:03:22,040
which is already enough for a show.

52
00:03:22,106 --> 00:03:31,345
[Music]

53
00:03:31,411 --> 00:03:35,157
There are several ways to enter the trick
from the pedals or the cranks.

54
00:03:35,590 --> 00:03:40,091
The most common way
is to do a "unispin 90",

55
00:03:40,263 --> 00:03:43,997
which means turning the unicycle
a quarter turn to land on the tire.

56
00:03:49,621 --> 00:03:53,428
Once you're at ease hopping on the tire,
it should come pretty quickly.

57
00:03:53,561 --> 00:03:55,257
Technically, it's not that complicated:

58
00:03:55,634 --> 00:03:58,954
you start from the pedals
with your small hops,

59
00:03:59,033 --> 00:04:05,654
"seat out", and when you want
to hop onto the tire,

60
00:04:05,720 --> 00:04:08,280
you hop a little higher
and turn the unicycle a quarter turn.

61
00:04:11,594 --> 00:04:15,702
The easiest grip is to hold the unicycle
like this during your small hops,

62
00:04:15,774 --> 00:04:18,567
and then just give it a quarter turn.

63
00:04:22,524 --> 00:04:23,865
Your body stays on the same axis:

64
00:04:24,096 --> 00:04:26,343
it's the unicycle
that does the quarter turn.

65
00:04:26,367 --> 00:04:28,517
The reverse works too,
but it's not the same trick.

66
00:04:34,097 --> 00:04:36,018
This "unispin" entry can be scary,

67
00:04:36,042 --> 00:04:39,018
but it's not that hard
once you have the basics down.

68
00:04:39,263 --> 00:04:42,670
Here again, get someone
to hold you at the hips.

69
00:04:44,731 --> 00:04:48,164
Another way into this trick,
a very smooth, freestyle one,

70
00:04:48,423 --> 00:04:51,931
is to block the fork
and the wheel with your foot,

71
00:04:52,377 --> 00:04:55,271
and that way, you can lean on it,

72
00:04:55,344 --> 00:04:57,890
it's solid enough to turn
your body a quarter turn.

73
00:04:57,956 --> 00:05:06,008
[Music]

74
00:05:06,074 --> 00:05:08,341
So you block with your first foot here,

75
00:05:08,388 --> 00:05:10,195
which lets you take
the second one off the wheel,

76
00:05:10,367 --> 00:05:13,980
place it, then just turn your foot
and you're in position.

77
00:05:16,087 --> 00:05:18,848
To get out of the trick
and back onto the pedals

78
00:05:19,274 --> 00:05:24,655
from the wheel, I think the easiest way
is to do a "90 unispin".

79
00:05:24,914 --> 00:05:27,620
It takes you from the wheel
down to the pedals.

80
00:05:27,686 --> 00:05:38,971
[Music]

81
00:05:39,037 --> 00:05:40,685
Once you're comfortable with all of that,

82
00:05:40,716 --> 00:05:46,110
you can come up with other ways
into the trick and other ways out.

83
00:05:46,176 --> 00:05:55,588
[Music]

84
00:05:55,654 --> 00:05:59,408
Of course, beyond this trick,
you've had a first look at "unispins".

85
00:05:59,814 --> 00:06:03,181
Starting from the 90,
you can imagine all the rest: 180,

86
00:06:03,234 --> 00:06:05,580
270, 360, and so on.

87
00:06:05,646 --> 00:06:20,940
[Music]

